K1       THE TYPE OF THE WALL -- re-derived, not cited
         S = -CS*k - Vol*sigma
         S == -CS*k - Vol*sigma : True
         dS/dk = -CS   == -CS : True
         Brown-Henneaux + sigma = ell/4G  =>  c = 6*sigma   == 6 sigma : True
         [sigma] = [ell/4G] = 1/4 x (length)^0  -> length drops out: True
         [c] = [6 sigma] -> dimensionless: True; [k] integer level -> dimensionless
         B1015's DECLARATION names A2 = c = 6 sigma 'the one continuous
         DIMENSIONLESS external coupling', and A1 = ell as the one from which
         NO DIMENSIONLESS NUMBER FLOWS.  The wall is therefore about a
         DIMENSIONLESS quantity.
K1 PASS  THE SEAT'S OWN SENTENCE IS WRONG: it gave the wall's type
         as dimensionful.  Both of the action's couplings are dimensionless, and
         the anchor that stays free (A2 = c = 6 sigma) is the dimensionless one.

