K4       THE MECHANISM -- CS multiplicativity, with a NON-VACUOUS control
         m004   CS=               0.0  rational: 0
         m003   CS=              0.25  rational: 1/4
         m202   CS=   0.0833333333333  rational: 1/12
         m015   CS=   -0.153204133297  rational: NO (control)
         covers tested: 12;  CS(cover) == deg*CS(base) mod 1/2 and vol multiplicative: 12 of 12
         CONTROL m015 (chiral, off the family): CS rational? NO  <- the instrument does NOT rationalise everything
K4 PASS  multiplicativity holds.  THE DERIVATION IT LICENSES:
         if M and N share a finite cover C, of degrees a over M and b over N,
         then a*CS(M) = CS(C) = b*CS(N) mod 1/2.  With CS(m004) = 0 this forces
         b*CS(N) = 0 mod 1/2 for every N commensurable with m004 -- CS(N) is
         TORSION, hence rational with denominator dividing 2b.  The family's
         rationality is not an observation; it is FORCED BY m004's OWN ZERO.

