K5 PARTIAL -- and the partiality is the finding.  99 of 112 members are
         arithmetic, hence commensurable with PSL(2,O_3) and with m004, and K4's
         derivation is LICENSED on those 99.  THE OTHER 13 ARE NOT
         COMMENSURABLE WITH m004: B1186's 112-family, defined by the SHAPE FIELD, is
         NOT a single commensurability class.  An imaginary-quadratic invariant trace
         field does not imply arithmeticity -- integral traces are a second condition,
         and 13 members fail it.  THIS CORRECTS A READING THE RECORD RELIES ON.
         AND THE ANOMALY IS REPORTED, NOT HIDDEN: all 13 non-arithmetic members
         STILL have 24*CS integral, which K4's mechanism does NOT explain.  The
         explanation that does cover them is the one this arc CITES and does not
         re-derive: B(Q(sqrt(-3))) tensor Q has rank r_2 = 1, so every member's Bloch
         invariant is a RATIONAL multiple of one generator's, forcing rational CS from
         the SHAPE FIELD alone (Neumann-Yang, Bloch invariants of hyperbolic
         3-manifolds).  K4's commensurability route is then a special case.  FLAGGED
         AS CITED, NOT VERIFIED HERE.
         ALSO REPORTED per the seal's own rule: explicit common covers were found for
         2 of 4 probed members and NOT for the chiral ones at degree <= 6 over
         m004, so the licence rests on the certificate, not on a constructed cover.

