K6 PASS  THE LAW HOLDS: CS(b+-W) - CS(b++W) = 1/4 mod 1/2 for EVERY
         once-punctured-torus word tested.  The b++/b+- sign is the -I bit -- the
         SAME Z/2 that separates m004 from m003, and the same one xB007 found the
         character variety blind to.  Through dS/dk = -CS it shifts the action by
         exactly -k/4: a quantized Z/4 phase in the level.

K7       DOES ANY OF THIS CROSS THE WALL?  (blind cell; declared prior: NO)
         What would count, per the seal: a numerical value for c or sigma derived
         from the family's own data with no new input.
         The attempt, stated so it can be checked:
           S = -CS*k - Vol*sigma, CS in (1/24)Z on the family, Vol in 12*v0*Z.
           The CS index is an INTEGER mod 12; sigma is a CONTINUOUS positive real.
           No equation in the family's data relates them: the index constrains the
           k-term only, and k is a free integer.  Setting the index to any value
           leaves sigma completely undetermined.
         crossing exhibited: False
K7 NEGATIVE  THE WALL STANDS FOR sigma.  What DOES change is its GROUND:
         B1015 prices A2 on 'the object is provably blind to the quantized level k'.
         K2/K6 show that blindness is m004's INDEX VALUE 0, not a property of the
         object's family -- 65 of the 112 members have CS != 0 and DO see k.  The
         wall's justification is an AXIOM (A5, which picks the branch), not a
         derivation.  That is a REFRAMING, and by the seal's own rule it is a LEAD,
         not an upgrade.

